From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:14:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 63/63] Database: a lost database is retried every 5 seconds;
 players are told, and the server stops if it stays away

When the database went away, every query tried to reconnect (twice), each waiting on the
connect, and the server kept running for good with nothing saved.

- DBcore::Reconnect returned the status itself, so a failed reconnect read as success. It
  returns true only when it connected.
- While the database can't be reached, a new connection is tried at most every 5 seconds; the
  queries in between fail at once with "The database can't be reached." and the
  "Status != Connected" lines aren't logged again for each one. A connect gives up after 5 s
  instead of the OS's TCP timeout. A query is retried once after a reconnect, not for ever.
- The log says when the database went away and when it's back, and for how long.
- After 10 seconds without it, players get a message that nothing they do is saved. If it
  isn't back within <database><haltAfterMinutes> (new, default 5; 0 keeps running), the server
  stops without its shutdown save (which would fail). Players are told when it's back.
- A failed market sim save is tried again at the next save time (30 s), not every second: an
  outage wrote about 170 log lines a second.

Tested natively against a MariaDB container: stopped for 25 s, the server carried on and said
"The database is back after 15 seconds."; stopped for good with haltAfterMinutes 1, the server
stopped itself after 60 s.
